# prospector reuses the same API keys as the geo-prospecting project.
# By default, prospector/.env is a symlink to geo-prospecting/.env so both
# tools share one set of credentials. If you want prospector to have its own
# .env instead, delete the symlink and copy the four keys below into a real
# file at this path.

SERPAPI_KEY=
COMPANIES_HOUSE_API_KEY=
# Primary business-discovery source (see places_client.py). SerpAPI above
# is used as an automatic fallback if this is unset or Places errors/returns
# 0 results, so it's not strictly required for the tool to run — but without
# it every discovery call pays for SerpAPI instead of the already-paid-for
# Places API.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
# Optional. The ad-spend module (Meta/Google ad checks via Apify) was
# removed in the "Prospector v2" rebuild's Phase 1 and this key is NOT used
# for that anymore. It's since been narrowly re-introduced for one thing
# only: enrichers/site.py's last-resort site-fetch fallback (layer 3 of 3,
# after httpx and Playwright both fail) via the `apify/rag-web-browser`
# actor. If unset, that fallback layer is simply skipped — no error, just
# thinner opportunity_score coverage on the handful of sites that block
# both httpx and a real headless browser. See README "Site-fetch
# escalation" for cost details.
APIFY_TOKEN=
